{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-117071",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the length of $AB$ by using the formula for the perimeter, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+CD+DA \\\\ p & =2AB+2BC \\\\ 36 & =2AB+2(10) \\\\ 36 & =2AB+20 \\\\ 2AB & =16 \\\\ AB & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =10\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
